\pard\sa240\f1\fs36 Memory Card Test\par
\pard\sa240\f0\fs24 Test your memory card speed and capacity, while detecting fakes.\par
\par
\f1\fs28 Opening the app on macOS\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs24 This app is not signed with an Apple Developer certificate, so the first time you open it macOS may say it "cannot be opened because Apple cannot check it for malicious software." This is expected. To open it:\par
\pard\sa120\li360\fs24 1.  Right-click (or Control-click) "Memory Card Test.app" and choose \f1 Open\f0 .\par
2.  In the dialog that appears, click \f1 Open\f0  again.\par
\pard\sa120\fs24 You only need to do this once. After that it opens normally by double-click.\par
\par
\f1\fs28 How to use it\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs24 Insert your memory card, select it from the list, choose a test, and click \f1 Start test\f0 :\par
\pard\sa120\li360\fs24 \'95  \f1 Quick speed test\f0  \'96 a fast read/write benchmark plus a basic integrity check.\par
\'95  \f1 Full capacity test\f0  \'96 fills the free space and reads every byte back; the most reliable way to confirm real capacity and catch fakes (can take a while on large cards).\par
\pard\sa120\fs24 Test data is written to a temporary folder on the card and deleted automatically when the test finishes or is stopped. Keep the card connected until it completes.\par
